          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS coordinates electronics recycling for Billings and surrounding Yellowstone County communities. Regional projects can also be planned across the broader eastern Montana trade area, depending on equipment volume, access requirements, and pickup logistics."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is available at no cost for qualifying volumes and approved service arrangements. Contact STS with equipment categories, approximate quantity, and collection details so the team can review the project and discuss scheduling."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to equipment after pickup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment is received, sorted, and directed through the appropriate reuse, recovery, or destruction pathway. Data-bearing devices receive the handling specified in the project plan, while recoverable materials move through documented downstream processing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS can provide service records and disposition documentation suited to the project. Organizations often use these records for asset closeout, procurement files, sustainability reporting, privacy reviews, and internal audit preparation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Scheduling depends on volume, access, equipment type, and route availability. Many projects can be arranged within the same week after the scope is confirmed. Larger refreshes may require coordination across departments or buildings."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What standards guide data sanitization?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "NIST SP 800-88 is a recognized reference for media sanitization. STS can discuss clear, purge, and destroy methods with your security or compliance team, then document the selected approach for the equipment included in your project."
          }
        }
